# Tome of the Dead DEC1 dead skeleton BONES floor decor (concept-screen §3.3 "Dead skeleton, BONES (DEC1)").
# DRAFT for user review (2026-10-19). Format = tools/tiles_convert.py block ("=== name WxH cells:..."),
# '#' ink, '.' paper, MSB-left. 32x8 = 4 cells x 1 row, standing row 7, every cell $47
# (bright white ink, black paper): one ink, black paper -> clash-legal by construction.
# Silhouette condensed from skeleton_collapsed (sprites/grid) to a lying pose: skull (left,
# jaw on the floor line), spine row 6 crossing every cell edge (cols 7|8, 15|16, 23|24 touch so
# the 4 glyphs read as one pile), 4 rib arcs, pelvis, femur (right). Fixed facing, no mirror.
# Cell -> common tile id (screen order, NOT contiguous -> BONES_IDS table):
#   cols  0- 7 = id 13 (bones_0, skull)    cols  8-15 = id 15 (bones_1, ribs)
#   cols 16-23 = id 16 (bones_2, ribs/hip) cols 24-31 = id 31 (bones_3, femur)
